    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the full test suite is green (3/3 tests pass, `BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the optional, validated `postcode` field for owners:\n\n**1. API contract (`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`)** \u2014 Added an optional `postcode` property to the `OwnerFields` schema with `pattern: \"^[0-9]{4}$\"`. Since the project generates DTOs with `performBeanValidation=true`, a non-4-digit value (e.g. `\"12\"`) is rejected as a `400` via bean validation before it reaches the controller.\n\n**2. Domain model (`Owner.java`)** \u2014 Added a `postcode` column with getter/setter. MapStruct auto-maps it on both `OwnerFieldsDto \u2192 Owner` (store) and `Owner \u2192 OwnerDto` (return), since the field names match.\n\n**3. Range validation (`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`)** \u2014 Added `validatePostcode(...)`, called during create. When a postcode is present it:\n   - re-checks the 4-digit shape (defensive, independent of the generated annotation),\n   - derives the region by reusing the existing `OwnerLocality.forCity(...)` table (Sydney\u2192NSW, etc.),\n   - rejects with `400` (`InvalidOwnerFieldsException`, `errors: [\"postcode\"]`) when the value is outside the region's range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099).\n   - A city with no known region (\"UNKNOWN\") accepts any 4-digit postcode; an absent postcode is accepted unchanged, keeping the request contract backward-compatible.\n\n**4. Persistence** \u2014 Added the `postcode` column to all four `schema.sql` files (h2/hsqldb/mysql/postgres) and fixed the positional owner seed inserts in `hsqldb/data.sql` (the test profile) by adding the extra `NULL` \u2014 all seed rows have NULL trailing columns so position is immaterial.\n\nThe three new acceptance tests pass: valid postcode stored/returned, owner without postcode accepted, and malformed postcode rejected with 400. The spec's out-of-range-for-known-region rejection is also wired in even though no test directly exercises it.",
